# Infrastructure Access

Checkpoint-based evaluation is configured for GPUs with approximately
24 GB of GPU memory. This capacity may not be consistently available
in common public environments such as standard Google Colab sessions.

Evaluators may use any compatible infrastructure. As an optional
fallback, the authors can provide temporary SSH access to an isolated
evaluation server.

Temporary access credentials will be provided only through ACSAC
HotCRP and will remain valid during the artifact evaluation period.

## Connect to the Provided Server

The server address, SSH port, username, and temporary password are
provided privately through ACSAC HotCRP.

```bash
ssh mario_aec@<server-address>
```

Enter the temporary password when prompted.

## Start an Evaluation Session

The provided server already has Miniconda and the `mario` environment
installed. Do not rerun `./install.sh`; activate the environment at the start
of each SSH session:

```bash
cd ~/MARIO
conda activate mario
```

If `conda` is not found, initialize it in the current shell and retry:

```bash
source "$HOME/miniconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh"
conda activate mario
```

All required datasets and release checkpoints are preloaded. Evaluators
do not need sudo access and do not need to install or download additional
files. Run each claim script as described in the
[Artifact Evaluation section](../README.md#artifact-evaluation).
